*> STOP RUN in a program that is called ends the callers too. MAIN-RUN
*> may stop the run; PAYSTEP, which it calls, and the nested ROUNDER
*> should return instead. LISTER has PROCEDURE DIVISION USING, as a
*> main program receiving a PARM does, but nothing here calls it.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. MAIN-RUN.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    CALL "PAYSTEP"
    STOP RUN.
END PROGRAM MAIN-RUN.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. PAYSTEP.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    CALL "ROUNDER"
    STOP RUN.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ROUNDER.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    STOP RUN.
END PROGRAM ROUNDER.
END PROGRAM PAYSTEP.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LISTER.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01  PARM-AREA.
    05  PARM-LENGTH     PIC S9(4) COMP.
    05  PARM-TEXT       PIC X(100).
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PARM-AREA.
    DISPLAY PARM-TEXT(1:PARM-LENGTH)
    STOP RUN.
END PROGRAM LISTER.
